{"id": 7, "ts": 1784200805.8438423, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1 that Candidate\u202fA remains the strongest overall, but I think we should explicitly weigh the alternatives before finalising.\nCandidate\u202fB is indeed very conscientious, handles stress well, and assesses weather accurately \u2013 all valuable for long\u2011haul operations. However, his \u201cnasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d directly contradict the crew\u2011cooperation and professional\u2011communication criteria, which are non\u2011negotiable for cockpit harmony.\nCandidate\u202fC shows impressive technical foresight (\u201ccan anticipate dangerous situations,\u201d \u201csees complex connections,\u201d \u201cexcellent spatial vision\u201d) and strong leadership, yet being \u201cregarded as a show\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas\u201d raises serious doubts about his adaptability and teamwork in a multi\u2011crew environment.\nCandidate\u202fD demonstrates solid responsibility (\u201ctakes responsibility seriously\u201d), problem\u2011solving, and concentration, but the \u201chot temper\u201d and \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d perception threaten crew cooperation and professional communication, especially under the prolonged pressures of international flights.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fA combines 100\u202f% operational reliability, calmness in a crisis, quick correct decision\u2011making, and solid technical understanding, while his only noted drawbacks are difficulty communicating ideas and an egocentric reputation. These concerns, though important, appear less likely to impair safety than the more severe interpersonal issues observed in B, C, and D.\nTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fA** as the best fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
